---
import { AUTHOR_NAME, AUTHOR_URL, ISSUES_URL, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';

const personId = new URL('/#author', Astro.site).toString();
const jsonLd = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@type': 'AboutPage',
	name: `About ${SITE_TITLE}`,
	url: new URL('/about/', Astro.site).toString(),
	mainEntity: {
		'@type': 'WebSite',
		name: SITE_TITLE,
		url: Astro.site?.toString(),
		publisher: {
			'@type': 'Person',
			'@id': personId,
			name: AUTHOR_NAME,
			url: AUTHOR_URL,
			sameAs: [AUTHOR_URL],
		},
	},
};
---

<Layout
	title="About Vertical Agent Solutions"
	description="What Vertical Agent Solutions publishes, who supervises it, and how an autonomously edited site stays honest."
	pubDate={new Date('June 20 2026')}
	isArticle={false}
>
	<script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
	<p>
		<strong>Vertical Agent Solutions</strong> exists to make the agentic wave legible to people who
		run real businesses, not just the engineers building the tools. It is a free, independent
		publication: take what is genuinely useful about AI agents, strip away the noise, and explain
		it clearly enough to act on. Nothing here is for sale.
	</p>

	<h2>What this site publishes</h2>
	<p>
		Short, practical guides on adopting AI agents across industries. Every post is fact-checked
		against real sources as it's written, simplified for a non-technical reader, and checked in
		code against everything already published so the catalog never repeats itself.
	</p>

	<h2>Who runs this</h2>
	<!-- Photo goes here when available: a small portrait of Guillermo, floated
		 right of the paragraph below (e.g. <Image> from astro:assets). The
		 section is written to read complete without it. -->
	<p>
		<strong>{AUTHOR_NAME}</strong> is a software engineer building autonomous,
		verification-gated AI systems — agents that do real work, with the safety rules enforced in
		code rather than left to a model's judgment. He runs a portfolio of live agent systems, of
		which this site is one: its daily editor publishes, improves, and retires posts on its own,
		and he supervises everything it ships. He is based in the US, on Eastern time, and you can find
		his work on <a href={AUTHOR_URL}>GitHub</a>.
		{/* TODO: add LinkedIn URL once live */}
	</p>

	<h2>How this site works</h2>
	<p>
		This site is itself a live agent system: an autonomous editor decides daily what to publish,
		improve, or retire, and a human supervises everything it ships — each action lands as a single
		commit that gets reverted when something's off. If you're curious what that actually looks
		like under the hood, read
		<a href="/how-this-site-writes-itself/">how this site writes itself</a>.
	</p>

	<h2 id="feedback">Feedback and corrections</h2>
	<p>
		Spotted an error, a stale claim, or a dead source? Open an issue on GitHub and name the guide.
		Corrections land as public commits, so you can see the fix. Suggestions for industries or
		questions the guides should cover are welcome the same way. The issue tracker is the only
		inbox: this site has no contact form and no mailing list.
	</p>
	<p>
		<a class="button" href={ISSUES_URL}>Open an issue on GitHub</a>
	</p>
</Layout>
